1
00:00:08,980 --> 00:00:13,900
(This story is entirely fictional)

2
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:32,340
(Based on the novel
Doctor Qin: Executer)

3
00:00:33,520 --> 00:00:34,640
Don't be scared, Keke.

4
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:36,400
It's me.

5
00:00:39,760 --> 00:00:40,560
Don't be afraid.

6
00:00:41,640 --> 00:00:42,920
The nightmare is over.

7
00:01:11,960 --> 00:01:14,120
Hi, Executer.

8
00:01:18,100 --> 00:01:22,100
=Doctor Qin: Executer=
=Episode 18=

9
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:26,840
Who's the man in this painting?

10
00:01:28,320 --> 00:01:29,120
It's me.

11
00:01:33,880 --> 00:01:35,240
That was back in high school.

12
00:01:35,640 --> 00:01:39,280
So this sketch book
has both current surveillance

13
00:01:39,640 --> 00:01:41,040
and old memories?

14
00:01:51,880 --> 00:01:52,640
Wen, hurry up.

15
00:01:52,640 --> 00:01:53,640
The sun's going down.

16
00:01:53,640 --> 00:01:54,400
Okay. Okay.

17
00:01:55,440 --> 00:01:56,200
Come on.

18
00:01:57,660 --> 00:01:59,070
Wow.

19
00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:01,840
Very good.

20
00:02:02,240 --> 00:02:03,480
This is totally amazing.

21
00:02:04,360 --> 00:02:05,160
Look.

22
00:02:07,640 --> 00:02:09,280
I think my composition's perfect.

23
00:02:09,720 --> 00:02:11,120
This looks terrible.

24
00:02:12,050 --> 00:02:12,600
Please,

25
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:13,880
I'm not a pro.

26
00:02:13,960 --> 00:02:15,080
It looks awful.

27
00:02:17,560 --> 00:02:18,400
I'll take a new one for you.

28
00:02:20,640 --> 00:02:21,520
Hey there.

29
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:23,280
Let me introduce you

30
00:02:23,280 --> 00:02:25,000
to a photographer with a magical touch.

31
00:02:26,930 --> 00:02:27,650
Hey,

32
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:29,320
just take it. We're losing the light.

33
00:02:29,480 --> 00:02:30,360
Come on, Xia Wen.

34
00:02:30,360 --> 00:02:32,480
I'll get you a drink
you'll never forget.

35
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:34,000
Let's go.

36
00:02:36,080 --> 00:02:36,880
What are you doing?

37
00:02:42,160 --> 00:02:42,960
Hey,

38
00:02:43,640 --> 00:02:45,720
can you shift a little?

39
00:02:45,840 --> 00:02:47,200
It'll make the photo look more natural.

40
00:03:38,080 --> 00:03:38,840
Then

41
00:03:40,560 --> 00:03:42,240
my father passed away
from stomach cancer.

42
00:03:43,640 --> 00:03:44,680
I was a total mess.

43
00:03:46,160 --> 00:03:47,200
(I stopped going to school.)

44
00:03:47,480 --> 00:03:48,280
(I felt like...)

45
00:03:48,840 --> 00:03:50,840
(I felt like the whole world
had turned gray.)

46
00:03:51,520 --> 00:03:52,480
(Nothing mattered.)

47
00:03:55,280 --> 00:03:56,080
(It was her.)

48
00:03:56,920 --> 00:03:58,120
(She kept writing me letters.)

49
00:04:01,140 --> 00:04:01,700
(Norwegian Wood by Murakami Haruki)

50
00:04:01,700 --> 00:04:04,860
(All The Best)

51
00:04:25,480 --> 00:04:26,680
(Sometimes, they were just jokes.)

52
00:04:27,880 --> 00:04:28,680
(Sometimes,)

53
00:04:29,680 --> 00:04:30,520
(they were doodles.)

54
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:32,440
(She just slowly)

55
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:34,680
(pulled me out of it,)

56
00:04:35,760 --> 00:04:37,000
(bit by bit.)

57
00:04:43,440 --> 00:04:44,480
I really wish...

58
00:04:46,480 --> 00:04:48,400
I really wish she wasn't the Executer.

59
00:04:58,560 --> 00:05:00,920
Mr. Dong, since I have
a personal connection to the suspect,

60
00:05:01,520 --> 00:05:02,360
I'm asking to be recused.

61
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:05,040
Request approved, Qin Ming.

62
00:05:07,120 --> 00:05:08,120
I get it.

63
00:05:08,800 --> 00:05:09,600
Alright then.

64
00:05:10,200 --> 00:05:11,800
Take a minute to get your head straight.

65
00:05:14,320 --> 00:05:15,120
Okay.

66
00:05:15,600 --> 00:05:16,400
Back to work!

67
00:05:16,960 --> 00:05:17,760
Mr. Dong!

68
00:05:18,720 --> 00:05:19,520
She's awake.

69
00:05:20,160 --> 00:05:21,160
Zhang Lanfen's awake!

70
00:05:22,160 --> 00:05:23,440
Let's head to the hospital.

71
00:05:46,720 --> 00:05:47,560
Ms. Zhang!

72
00:05:50,040 --> 00:05:50,880
Ms. Zhang!

73
00:05:54,800 --> 00:05:55,640
Dr. Chen!

74
00:06:04,760 --> 00:06:07,720
It's acute post-traumatic
stress disorder.

75
00:06:07,960 --> 00:06:09,360
She won't speak or respond to anything.

76
00:06:09,600 --> 00:06:10,880
Every time we took the restraints off,

77
00:06:10,880 --> 00:06:12,160
she'd go completely wild,

78
00:06:12,400 --> 00:06:14,440
scratching at every surface
over and over with her nails.

79
00:06:17,560 --> 00:06:18,920
So I gave her a pen and some paper.

80
00:06:36,120 --> 00:06:37,400
These are...

81
00:06:38,240 --> 00:06:40,120
These are sketches of the crime scenes.

82
00:06:41,680 --> 00:06:43,280
How does she know all these details?

83
00:06:58,640 --> 00:07:00,240
(Humiliation)
(When I was locked up there,)

84
00:07:00,840 --> 00:07:02,440
(Jin Keke was really down one day.)

85
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:05,160
(She told me everything.)

86
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:06,680
(Serve the People with Dedication)
(Every person she killed.)

87
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:08,360
(And all her past with Qin Ming.)

88
00:07:08,440 --> 00:07:09,640
(She said)

89
00:07:09,960 --> 00:07:11,560
(she needed someone to witness it all.)

90
00:07:16,840 --> 00:07:17,640
The weather

91
00:07:19,240 --> 00:07:20,480
was perfect that day.

92
00:07:21,720 --> 00:07:24,080
I was out by the door
watering the flowers.

93
00:07:25,400 --> 00:07:26,880
Jin Keke showed up.

94
00:07:28,120 --> 00:07:29,320
She smiled at me.

95
00:07:29,800 --> 00:07:30,600
Then

96
00:07:32,880 --> 00:07:34,760
she handed me an orange.

97
00:07:38,080 --> 00:07:39,880
(Said she brought it from her hometown,)

98
00:07:41,200 --> 00:07:42,000
(and that it was so sweet.)

99
00:07:44,160 --> 00:07:44,960
Next thing...

100
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:49,120
I felt like I fell straight
into a black hole.

101
00:07:50,480 --> 00:07:52,320
(Everything was spinning nonstop.)

102
00:07:52,840 --> 00:07:55,080
(I couldn't see or hear a thing.)

103
00:07:57,880 --> 00:07:58,880
I know for sure

104
00:08:00,360 --> 00:08:01,680
I wasn't asleep.

105
00:08:03,520 --> 00:08:04,320
It was...

106
00:08:06,520 --> 00:08:07,320
a collapse.

107
00:08:13,120 --> 00:08:13,920
Don't be scared.

108
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:17,160
You're safe here.

109
00:08:18,480 --> 00:08:20,040
No one's gonna bother us.

110
00:08:22,200 --> 00:08:24,120
Do you know why you're here?

111
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:27,800
Because

112
00:08:29,480 --> 00:08:31,280
you saw something you shouldn't have.

113
00:08:35,160 --> 00:08:37,320
I know.

114
00:08:38,600 --> 00:08:41,760
She's the exact model in my painting.

115
00:08:51,480 --> 00:08:52,320
Anyone out there?

116
00:09:00,250 --> 00:09:04,100
(In Memory of Xia Wen)

117
00:09:07,880 --> 00:09:08,720
Anyone there?

118
00:09:08,840 --> 00:09:09,720
Hello? Anyone?

119
00:09:09,760 --> 00:09:10,560
Help!

120
00:09:10,640 --> 00:09:11,920
Help! Somebody help!

121
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:13,560
Help...

122
00:09:14,360 --> 00:09:15,160
Help me.

123
00:09:15,680 --> 00:09:16,560
You're awake.

124
00:09:21,240 --> 00:09:22,160
Who are you?

125
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:23,120
What do you want?

126
00:09:24,400 --> 00:09:25,880
I'm the record keeper here.

127
00:09:27,080 --> 00:09:27,880
And you

128
00:09:29,120 --> 00:09:30,560
are about to become

129
00:09:31,680 --> 00:09:32,720
the new witness.

130
00:09:35,680 --> 00:09:36,480
Keke.

131
00:09:38,160 --> 00:09:39,160
Just let me go.

132
00:09:55,600 --> 00:09:56,880
(She tied me up,)

133
00:09:58,040 --> 00:09:59,520
(but she never hurt me.)

134
00:10:00,800 --> 00:10:02,520
(Even gave me food and water.)

135
00:10:02,880 --> 00:10:04,680
(But being in a place like that)

136
00:10:04,960 --> 00:10:06,560
(was a torture in itself.)

137
00:10:12,280 --> 00:10:13,080
Torture?

138
00:10:14,160 --> 00:10:15,240
What did you see?

139
00:10:17,800 --> 00:10:18,960
The final judgment.

140
00:10:25,720 --> 00:10:26,520
Sometimes,

141
00:10:31,400 --> 00:10:35,040
she'd stare at that wall
covered in photos...

142
00:10:37,640 --> 00:10:38,560
(for a long time.)

143
00:10:45,880 --> 00:10:46,680
(Sometimes,)

144
00:10:47,840 --> 00:10:48,960
she'd just sit there,

145
00:10:49,760 --> 00:10:51,960
like she had a million things
on her mind.

146
00:10:53,160 --> 00:10:54,240
She'd stay there.

147
00:10:55,040 --> 00:10:55,840
For ages.

148
00:10:57,040 --> 00:10:57,840
Sometimes,

149
00:11:00,800 --> 00:11:02,760
she'd say a few things to me.

150
00:11:03,600 --> 00:11:04,920
I never answered.

151
00:11:08,400 --> 00:11:10,320
She didn't even need me to.

152
00:11:11,840 --> 00:11:13,720
She just wanted to make a sound,

153
00:11:14,680 --> 00:11:16,520
to prove she was still alive.

154
00:11:43,360 --> 00:11:45,120
This is the first person I killed.

155
00:11:47,440 --> 00:11:48,240
Su Shi.

156
00:11:49,400 --> 00:11:51,680
(She spent her whole life
trying to control others.)

157
00:11:52,320 --> 00:11:54,640
(She treated her daughter
as an extension of herself,)

158
00:11:55,200 --> 00:11:57,000
(a piece she could beat, shape,)

159
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:58,960
(and show off however she wanted.)

160
00:11:59,280 --> 00:12:00,080
(So,)

161
00:12:00,280 --> 00:12:01,960
(the perfect judgment for her)

162
00:12:02,160 --> 00:12:03,840
(was to die at the hands
of the one piece)

163
00:12:03,840 --> 00:12:06,320
(she could never control,
the biggest failure she ever made.)

164
00:12:10,120 --> 00:12:11,720
This is the second person I killed.

165
00:12:12,880 --> 00:12:13,920
Le Tianyi.

166
00:12:14,480 --> 00:12:15,720
(He groveled before power.)

167
00:12:16,360 --> 00:12:18,120
(For every bit of humiliation
he suffered,)

168
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:20,080
(he would take it out
a thousand times worse)

169
00:12:20,080 --> 00:12:21,720
(on his wife, who's weaker than him.)

170
00:12:22,400 --> 00:12:23,880
(He didn't deserve to be called human.)

171
00:12:24,320 --> 00:12:25,120
(So,)

172
00:12:25,520 --> 00:12:27,560
(I put him
through the meat grinder myself)

173
00:12:28,120 --> 00:12:29,840
(and turned him into feed.)

174
00:12:30,600 --> 00:12:32,800
It's fair, isn't it?

175
00:12:33,680 --> 00:12:35,440
This is the fourth person I killed.

176
00:12:36,640 --> 00:12:37,680
Liu Sanhao.

177
00:12:43,680 --> 00:12:47,160
Liu Sanhao used violence
to drive my father to his death.

178
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:52,240
He destroyed so many other families
the exact same way.

179
00:12:52,520 --> 00:12:55,520
So I put together the craziest,

180
00:12:56,080 --> 00:12:57,440
most brutal show of violence

181
00:12:58,160 --> 00:12:59,680
just for him.

182
00:13:01,120 --> 00:13:02,520
I wanted him to feel

183
00:13:02,960 --> 00:13:05,360
(what it was like
to be tied up, beaten,)

184
00:13:05,480 --> 00:13:07,400
burned by scalding hot oil.

185
00:13:10,960 --> 00:13:11,960
Then

186
00:13:13,160 --> 00:13:16,160
I dropped him from way up high,

187
00:13:18,160 --> 00:13:19,200
so he could feel

188
00:13:21,120 --> 00:13:22,920
the exact same despair
my father felt back then.

189
00:13:26,760 --> 00:13:27,800
You get art.

190
00:13:29,840 --> 00:13:31,200
Do you like my judgments?

191
00:13:46,480 --> 00:13:47,280
Eat.

192
00:13:49,040 --> 00:13:50,400
I've got plenty more stories.

193
00:14:05,640 --> 00:14:07,000
(I don't know why)

194
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:09,760
(such a pretty girl)

195
00:14:10,240 --> 00:14:11,520
would kill so many people.

196
00:14:12,120 --> 00:14:13,880
She judged every single one of them

197
00:14:14,200 --> 00:14:15,520
with brutal methods!

198
00:14:16,200 --> 00:14:17,000
And she

199
00:14:18,120 --> 00:14:19,160
was so cold

200
00:14:20,160 --> 00:14:20,960
and calm about it.

201
00:14:22,120 --> 00:14:23,560
Who's the third victim?

202
00:14:24,600 --> 00:14:26,160
That's terrifying.

203
00:14:43,360 --> 00:14:45,200
You're the most despicable collector

204
00:14:46,160 --> 00:14:47,880
in the whole world.

205
00:14:51,040 --> 00:14:53,200
You've hoarded the crushing pain

206
00:14:53,200 --> 00:14:55,440
of every single girl.

207
00:15:13,400 --> 00:15:15,920
Didn't you love the starlight dance?

208
00:15:16,560 --> 00:15:19,120
Jin Xiaoxue, just forgive me.

209
00:15:19,120 --> 00:15:20,320
Dance for me.

210
00:15:22,280 --> 00:15:23,320
Dance for me.

211
00:15:24,760 --> 00:15:27,480
Forgive me, I'm begging you.

212
00:15:27,480 --> 00:15:28,120
Dance!

213
00:15:30,520 --> 00:15:33,160
Isn't this exactly how
you treated us back then?

214
00:15:35,520 --> 00:15:37,160
Now it's your turn.

215
00:15:40,720 --> 00:15:41,400
Move it.

216
00:15:41,640 --> 00:15:44,120
Jin Xiaoxue, I'll kill you!

217
00:15:44,120 --> 00:15:44,960
I'll kill you!

218
00:15:48,170 --> 00:15:51,270
♪Back then, you and I turned away♪

219
00:15:52,330 --> 00:15:55,060
♪Silence swallowed the sound of crying♪

220
00:15:56,190 --> 00:15:58,730
♪The fading warmth on your cheek♪

221
00:15:59,820 --> 00:16:02,610
♪Chilled my soul to the bone♪

222
00:16:04,450 --> 00:16:07,430
♪The forever we once promised♪

223
00:16:08,220 --> 00:16:11,600
♪Shattered into dust in the wind♪

224
00:16:13,500 --> 00:16:17,090
♪Then I heard your name♪

225
00:16:17,410 --> 00:16:20,920
♪Like thunder hits my heart♪

226
00:16:21,340 --> 00:16:24,730
♪The warmth I once kept hidden♪

227
00:16:24,910 --> 00:16:28,390
♪Turned to dust♪

228
00:16:28,390 --> 00:16:34,590
♪I love you,
but it's a love I'll never have♪

229
00:16:35,980 --> 00:16:42,880
♪The wild wind swept away
all the warmth♪

230
00:16:43,410 --> 00:16:50,150
♪I love you,
but it's a love I'll never have♪

231
00:16:51,380 --> 00:16:54,920
♪When we meet again,
there's nothing but silence and tears♪

232
00:16:54,920 --> 00:16:55,720
Qin Ming.

233
00:16:57,800 --> 00:16:58,800
You're looking for me.

234
00:16:59,800 --> 00:17:00,560
Right?

235
00:17:02,340 --> 00:17:08,200
♪I love you,
but it's a love I'll never have♪

236
00:17:09,810 --> 00:17:16,080
♪The wild wind swept away
all the warmth♪

237
00:17:17,250 --> 00:17:23,980
♪I love you,
but it's a love I'll never have♪

238
00:17:25,210 --> 00:17:30,730
♪When we meet again,
there's nothing but silence and tears♪

239
00:17:46,880 --> 00:17:49,530
♪You've long forgotten our old days♪

240
00:17:50,580 --> 00:17:53,660
♪Leaving me alone with broken traces♪

241
00:17:54,260 --> 00:17:56,710
♪No path to turn back to♪

242
00:17:57,060 --> 00:18:00,340
♪The bond scattered without a trace♪

243
00:18:03,100 --> 00:18:09,840
♪Time and years tore us apart♪

244
00:18:10,050 --> 00:18:16,660
♪This heart is broken, never to mend♪

245
00:18:17,330 --> 00:18:24,110
♪I love you,
but it's a love I'll never have♪

246
00:18:24,770 --> 00:18:31,230
♪The wild wind swept away
all the warmth♪

247
00:18:32,260 --> 00:18:38,830
♪I love you,
but it's a love I'll never have♪

248
00:18:40,110 --> 00:18:45,460
♪When we meet again,
there's nothing but silence and tears♪

249
00:18:47,730 --> 00:18:51,970
♪Sunset washes over the old wall♪

250
00:18:52,490 --> 00:18:56,610
♪Milk tea cools on the stone steps♪

251
00:18:56,850 --> 00:19:00,850
♪Sea wind tugs at your sleeve♪

252
00:19:01,330 --> 00:19:05,170
♪Unspoken words just flee and fade♪

253
00:19:14,170 --> 00:19:18,090
♪The marks on the desk
have faded yellow♪

254
00:19:18,090 --> 00:19:20,890
♪I turned around,
and a gunshot rang out♪

255
00:19:21,570 --> 00:19:25,210
♪No one can truly feel another's pain♪

256
00:19:25,210 --> 00:19:29,410
♪The wind is cold,
a fading shadow sways♪

257
00:19:29,410 --> 00:19:34,170
♪Tonight, I don't care
about the universe♪

258
00:19:34,170 --> 00:19:38,610
♪I only want to see this through
with you♪

259
00:19:39,210 --> 00:19:42,970
♪A bullet pierces the spring night♪
